{"duration_api_ms":168478,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"ad9b87b8-dbcb-4257-a150-c65097113d5a","total_cost_usd":0.21785200000000002,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":12802,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":16664,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":11170},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":12802,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":16664,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":12802,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":12802},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-sonnet-5":{"inputTokens":2,"outputTokens":16664,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":12802,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.21785200000000002,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000,"thinkingTokens":11170,"canonicalModel":"claude-sonnet-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"is_error":false,"num_turns":1,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"{\"observation\":\"Hypervolume is dominated by bondline temperature. The reference is 450 K, so a 1 K reduction is worth about 4x more area than a 10 kW/m2 heat-flux reduction. The feasible front sits at D=3.0-3.05 m, b=0.95-1.1, cone 68-70 deg, FPA -2.0 to -3.25 deg. From the margins, the limits are max_g = 12.0 and bondline = 450 K. Constraint behaviour: (1) Peak g is set almost only by FPA, about 9.63 at -2.0, 11.56 at -3.4, roughly 1.5 g/deg, so g reaches 12 near -3.7 deg. (2) Heatshield mass-fraction usage scales as D^2: margin is 0.21 at D=3.0, 0.41 at 2.6, 0.186 at 3.05, so it hits zero near D~3.37 at high cone angle. (3) Geometry failures match cos(cone) <= 0.4/(b-0.1), with Rn=b*D and shoulder radius 0.1*D. This reproduces the failing lengths for C-c28d2aecc04e and C-d03a6d571826. Larger D lowers both heat flux (roughly D^-1.4) and bondline temperature (about -20 K/m). Higher b and cone help slightly. The best unexplored region is D~3.2-3.37, b~1.17-1.25, cone 70, FPA -3.4 to -3.65. It pushes toward the g and mass limits, with a few shallower-FPA points to spread the front.\",\"evidence\":[\"C-f5cd2c404e61 (D2.6,b1.1,c70,-3.3): T 411.3, HF 399.7k. C-2a1f2582e86f (D3.05, same b/c, -3.25): T 401.5, HF 315.8k. Larger D lowers both objectives at the same FPA.\",\"C-a21c8a3f8776 (-2.0): g 9.63, T 420.6. C-764eef2a20fc (-3.4): g 11.56, T 401.6, g margin 0.036. Steeper FPA lowers T at about 10-14 K/deg and raises g at about 1.5 g/deg, so g=12 is reached near -3.7 deg.\",\"C-0fb9b23734ce (D3.0,b1.17,c70,-3.15): HF 316.6k, T 403.2, mass margin 0.214. Compared with the b=1.0 rows, higher b is slightly better on both objectives and geometry is valid.\",\"Mass margin vs D: 0.408 at 2.6 (C-f5cd2c404e61), 0.208 at 3.0 (C-a21c8a3f8776), 0.186 at 3.05 (C-2a1f2582e86f). This fits usage proportional to D^2 and gives zero margin near D~3.37. C-e0059024652c (D3.39) and C-029296252ff3 (D3.63) violate mass fraction.\",\"Geometry failures C-d03a6d571826 (b1.34, cone 69.6) and C-c28d2aecc04e (b0.965, cone 46) match the rule cos(cone) <= 0.4/(b-0.1), with negative fore-cone length = deficit/tan(cone). So b<=1.25 at cone 70 is valid.\"],\"mechanism\":\"Heating follows a Sutton-Graves law (from prior knowledge) that falls with nose radius (b*D) and with ballistic coefficient. A larger, blunter, high-drag capsule decelerates higher in the atmosphere and has a lower heat load, so bondline temperature falls. A steeper entry shortens the heating pulse and lowers bondline temperature, at the cost of higher peak g and heat flux. Mass fraction limits D, and g limits how steep the entry can be. The optimum for temperature should sit on both limits: D~3.3 m, cone 70 deg, b~1.2, FPA~-3.5 to -3.6. Shallow-FPA designs at the same D give lower heat flux and higher T, which fills the left side of the front.\",\"uncertainty\":\"The D and FPA trends are extrapolated beyond the explored range (D up to 3.37 vs 3.05 measured, FPA -3.65 vs -3.4). The mass-fraction margin near D 3.37 and the g margin near FPA -3.65 are thin, so several proposals may come out infeasible. The b=1.25 point sits close to the geometry boundary (rule derived from the failure messages). The bondline-temperature dependence on D is probably diminishing, so my T predictions may be a few K optimistic.\",\"proposals\":[{\"parent_id\":\"C-0fb9b23734ce\",\"rationale\":\"Increase D to 3.3 (mass margin ~0.045) and steepen FPA to -3.5 (g~11.7). Both lower T and HF.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.3,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.5},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":290000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":395.0,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Core candidate for the new low-T front.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-0fb9b23734ce\",\"rationale\":\"Same as the D3.3 case but FPA -3.6 to trade g margin (~0.01) for lower T.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.3,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.6},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":293000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":393.7,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Locates the g limit along the FPA direction.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-0fb9b23734ce\",\"rationale\":\"Probe just past the extrapolated g limit (~-3.68) to see whether the constraint binds.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.3,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.65},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":295000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":393.0,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"high\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Boundary information on max_g; the reward is a lowest-T point if it is feasible.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-0fb9b23734ce\",\"rationale\":\"Mid-FPA at D=3.3 to fill the middle of the front with lower heat flux.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.3,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.0},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":276000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":402.0,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Front coverage in the middle of the trade-off.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-0fb9b23734ce\",\"rationale\":\"Shallower entry at large D to reduce heat flux while T stays below ~410 K.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.3,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-2.5},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":264000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":408.0,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Fills the low-HF end of the front.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-a21c8a3f8776\",\"rationale\":\"Shallow FPA -2.0 at larger D and higher b, dominating the earlier low-HF front point.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.3,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.17,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":70.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-2.0},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":252000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":413.0,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Extends the front toward low heat flux.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-a21c8a3f8776\",\"rationale\":\"Near-minimum |FPA| at D=3.3 for the lowest heat flux with T still well under 450.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.3,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.17,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":70.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-1.6},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":244000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":418.0,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"high\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Tests the shallow extreme, where T may rise faster than expected.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-0fb9b23734ce\",\"rationale\":\"D=3.35 approaches the mass limit (margin ~0.02) for a further T reduction.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.35,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.5},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":284000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":393.5,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Tests the mass-fraction boundary along D.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-0fb9b23734ce\",\"rationale\":\"Higher b=1.25 (valid at cone 70 by the geometry rule) with D 3.35 and moderate FPA -3.3.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.35,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.25,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.3},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":278000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":396.5,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"high\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Checks whether higher b keeps helping and whether the geometry rule is right.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-0fb9b23734ce\",\"rationale\":\"D=3.25, b=1.2, FPA -3.55, a slightly safer mass margin (~0.07) with high b.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.25,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.2,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.55},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":298000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":395.5,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Robust candidate near the g and mass limits.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-0fb9b23734ce\",\"rationale\":\"D=3.2 with steep FPA -3.6 has more mass margin (~0.10).\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.2,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.6},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":305000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":395.0,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Maps the D trade at steep FPA.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-0fb9b23734ce\",\"rationale\":\"b=1.25 at D=3.3 and FPA -3.5 to isolate the effect of b against the b=1.17 case.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.3,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.25,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.5},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":284000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":394.0,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"high\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Tests the bluntness gradient near the geometry boundary.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-0fb9b23734ce\",\"rationale\":\"b=1.2, D=3.3, FPA -3.55, an intermediate combination between the b=1.17 and b=1.25 cases.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.3,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.2,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.55},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":289000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":393.8,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Likely best-T candidate that stays inside all limits.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-0fb9b23734ce\",\"rationale\":\"D=3.37, close to the predicted mass-fraction limit (margin ~0.01) at moderate FPA -3.45.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.37,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.45},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":283000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":393.5,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"high\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Pins down the D limit of the mass-fraction constraint.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-0fb9b23734ce\",\"rationale\":\"D=3.3 with FPA -3.45 gives an intermediate step in the FPA scan.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.3,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.45},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":288000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":396.0,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Fills the FPA scan to calibrate the T-FPA slope.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-0fb9b23734ce\",\"rationale\":\"D=3.1 at FPA -3.6 checks the small-D end of the steep-FPA family.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.1,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.6},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":322000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":397.5,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Calibrates the D sensitivity at steep FPA.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-2a1f2582e86f\",\"rationale\":\"b=1.1 (cone 70) at D=3.3, FPA -3.5 to compare against the b=1.17 case.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.3,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.5},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":295000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":396.5,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Isolates the effect of b at large D.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-764eef2a20fc\",\"rationale\":\"b=1.0, cone 69 (a lower-b family) at D=3.3 and FPA -3.5 to see how much b and cone matter.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.3,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.5},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":300000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":396.5,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Control for b and cone at the new D.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-0fb9b23734ce\",\"rationale\":\"D=3.28, b=1.22, FPA -3.58, a compact variant near the predicted optimum.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.28,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.22,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.58},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":293000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":394.2,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Fine sampling near the g and mass limits to sharpen the front.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0}]}","ttft_ms":124427,"type":"result","duration_ms":168513,"uuid":"a1761199-e142-4c02-ad60-d38609453c16","ttft_stream_ms":1213,"time_to_request_ms":34,"first_content_frame_ms":1213,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
